02.99 356.71 215.93 C 359.3 228.87 361.89 239.65 364.47 248.28 C 367.06 256.9 369.65 263.37 372.24 267.68 C 374.82 272 377.41 274.15 380 274.15 C 382.59 274.15 385.18 272 387.76 267.68 C 390.35 263.37 392.94 256.9 395.53 248.28 C 398.11 239.65 400.7 228.87 403.29 215.93 C 405.88 202.99 408.46 187.9 411.05 170.65 C 413.64 153.4 416.23 133.99 418.81 112.43 C 421.4 90.87 423.99 67.15 426.58 41.27\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#247456\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\" stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"266.15\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">y = x^2 - 4<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"333.42,320.73 426.58,134.42\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#d0a64a\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"219.58\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">y = 2x + 1<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"380,292.78 380,181\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#277da1\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"228.89\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">Axis: x = 0<\\/text><\\/g><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"377\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">x<\\/text><text x=\\\"12\\\" y=\\\"181\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\" transform=\\\"rotate(-90 12 181)\\\">y<\\/text><\\/svg><\\/div><p>Graph \\\\(y = x^2 - 4\\\\) and \\\\(y = 2x + 1\\\\) on the same axes. Identify the intersection points algebraically and verify them on the graph.<\\/p><\\/article><article class=\\\"presentation-slide-preview presentation-theme-modern presentation-template-lesson\\\"><header><span>SLIDE 04<\\/span><small>Mathematics · SHS Year 3<\\/small><\\/header><h4>4. Applying the concepts to a real‑life problem<\\/h4><ul><li>Translate a word problem into a quadratic equation.<\\/li><li>Use the axis of symmetry to find the maximum or minimum value.<\\/li><li>Solve any accompanying linear condition graphically.<\\/li><\\/ul><div class=\\\"presentation-visual presentation-visual-table\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><strong>Lesson visual<\\/strong><div class=\\\"presentation-visual-table-scroll\\\"><table><thead><tr><th>Step<\\/th><th>Action<\\/th><th>Result<\\/th><\\/tr><\\/thead><tbody><tr><td>1<\\/td><td>Write the quadratic function<\\/td><td>h = -0.5x^2 + 6<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>2<\\/td><td>Find axis of symmetry: x = -b\\/(2a) → x = 0<\\/td><td>Axis at x = 0<\\/td><\\/tr><tr><td>3<\\/td><td>Maximum height at vertex: h_max = 6<\\/td><td>Maximum height = 6 m<\\/td><\\/tr><\\/tbody><\\/table><\\/div><\\/div><p>Problem: A farmer designs a parabolic fence to enclose a field. The height of the fence at a distance \\\\(x\\\\) metres from the centre is given by \\\\(h = -0.5x^2 + 6\\\\). The gate is placed 2 m from the centre (linear condition \\\\(x = 2\\\\)). Determine the height of the fence at the gate and the maximum height of the fence.<\\/p><\\/article><article class=\\\"presentation-slide-preview presentation-theme-modern presentation-template-lesson\\\"><header><span>SLIDE 05<\\/span><small>Mathematics · SHS Year 3<\\/small><\\/header><h4>Slide 5 – Increasing &amp; Decreasing Intervals on a Quadratic Graph<\\/h4><ul><li>A quadratic function f(x)=ax²+bx+c forms a parabola.<\\/li><li>If a&lt;0 the parabola opens downward; the vertex is the maximum point.<\\/li><li>The function increases to the right of the vertex and decreases to the left.<\\/li><li>Identify the interval of increase (x &gt; h) and decrease (x &lt; h) where h is the x‑coordinate of the vertex.<\\/li><\\/ul><div class=\\\"presentation-visual presentation-visual-geometry\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><strong>Lesson visual<\\/strong><svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 720 380\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><defs><clipPath id=\\\"geometry-clip-95b5jzixhs\\\"><rect x=\\\"321.85\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" width=\\\"116.3\\\" height=\\\"314\\\"\\/><