<\\/text><text x=\\\"12\\\" y=\\\"181\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\" transform=\\\"rotate(-90 12 181)\\\">y<\\/text><\\/svg><\\/div><p>In pairs, plot the quadratic f(x) = -x² + 4 on graph paper. Mark the vertex and shade the region where the curve rises (right side) and falls (left side).<\\/p><\\/article><article class=\\\"presentation-slide-preview presentation-theme-modern presentation-template-lesson\\\"><header><span>SLIDE 06<\\/span><small>Mathematics · SHS Year 3<\\/small><\\/header><h4>Slide 6 – Positive &amp; Negative y‑Values (Range of y)<\\/h4><ul><li>The sign of y depends on whether the graph lies above or below the x‑axis.<\\/li><li>For f(x) = -x² + 4, the x‑intercepts occur where y = 0.<\\/li><li>Between the intercepts, y is positive; outside them, y is negative.<\\/li><\\/ul><div class=\\\"presentation-visual presentation-visual-geometry\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><strong>Lesson visual<\\/strong><svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 720 380\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><defs><clipPath id=\\\"geometry-clip-44to8jv9cd\\\"><rect x=\\\"321.85\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" width=\\\"116.3\\\" height=\\\"314\\\"\\/><\\/clipPath><\\/defs><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"321.85\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"24\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"321.85\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-5.62<\\/text><text x=\\\"313.85\\\" y=\\\"28\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">7.67<\\/text><line x1=\\\"350.93\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"350.93\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"102.5\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"102.5\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"350.93\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\