C 357 112.29 359.87 100.31 362.75 90.72 C 365.62 81.14 368.5 73.95 371.37 69.16 C 374.25 64.37 377.12 61.97 380 61.97 C 382.88 61.97 385.75 64.37 388.63 69.16 C 391.5 73.95 394.38 81.14 397.25 90.72 C 400.13 100.31 403 112.29 405.88 126.66 C 408.75 141.04 411.63 157.81 414.5 176.97 C 417.38 196.14 420.25 217.71 423.13 241.66 C 426 265.62 428.88 291.98 431.75 320.73\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#247456\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\" stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"53.97\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">y = -x² + 4<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"359.3,103.37 400.7,103.37\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#d0a64a\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"95.37\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">x‑axis<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"359.3,103.37 359.3,103.37\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#277da1\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"359.3\\\" y=\\\"95.37\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">Intercept (‑2,0)<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"400.7,103.37 400.7,103.37\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#c85845\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"400.7\\\" y=\\\"95.37\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">Intercept (2,0)<\\/text><\\/g><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"377\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">x<\\/text><text x=\\\"12\\\" y=\\\"181\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\" transform=\\\"rotate(-90 12 181)\\\">y<\\/text><\\/svg><\\/div><p>Using the same plotted graph, locate the points where the curve meets the x‑axis. Record the x‑values and discuss the intervals where the height (y) is positive versus negative.<\\/p><\\/article><article class=\\\"presentation-slide-preview presentation-theme-modern presentation-template-lesson\\\"><header><span>SLIDE 07<\\/span><small>Mathematics · SHS Year 3<\\/small><\\/header><h4>Slide 7 – Solving Related Equations Graphically<\\/h4><ul><li>A quadratic equation can be solved by locating its x‑intercepts on the graph.<\\/li><li>The quadratic formula gives the same solutions algebraically.<\\/li><li>Graphical solutions reinforce understanding of roots and their meaning.<\\/li><\\/ul><div class=\\\"presentation-visual presentation-visual-geometry\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><strong>Lesson visual<\\/strong><svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 720 380\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><defs><clipPath id=\\\"geometry-clip-w1tfnp3g7xr\\\"><rect x=\\\"321.85\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" width=\\\"116.3\\\" height=\\\"314\\\"\\/><\\/clipPath><\\/defs><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"321.85\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"24\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"321.85\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-5.62<\\/text><text x=\\\"313.85\\\" y=\\\"28\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">7.67<\\/text><line x1=\\\"350.93\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"350.93\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"102.5\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"102.5\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"350.93\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-2.81<\\/text><text x=\\\"313.85\\\" y=\\\"106.5\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">0.08<\\/text><line x1=\\\"380\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"380\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"181\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"181\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">0<\\/text><text x=\\\"313.85\\\" y=\\\"185\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-7.5<\\/text><line x1=\\\"409.07\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"409.07\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"259.5\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"259.5\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"409.07\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">2.81<\\/text><text x=\\\"313.85\\\" y=\\\"263.5\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-15.08<\\/text><line x1=\\\"438.15\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"338\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"438.15\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">5.62<\\/text><text x=\\\"313.85\\\" y=\\\"342\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-22.67<\\/text><line x1=\\\"380\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"380\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-axis\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"321.85\\\" y1=\\\"103.37\\\" x2=\\\"438.15\\\" y2=\\\"103.37\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-axis\\\"\\/><g clip-path=\\\"url(#geometry-clip-w1tfnp3g7xr)\\\"><path d=\\\"M 328.25 320.73 C 331.12 291.98 334 265.62 336.87 241.66 C 339.75 217.71 342.62 196.14 345.5 176.97 C 348.37 157.81 351.25 141.04 354.12 126.66 C 357 112.29 359.87 100.31 362.75 90.72 C 365.62 81.14 368.5 73.95 371.37 69.16 C 374.25 64.37 377.12 61.97 380 61.97 C 382.88 61.97 385.75 64.37 388.63 69.16 C 391.5 73.95 394.38 81.14 397.25 90.72 C 400.13 100.31 403 112.29 405.88 126.66 C 408.75 141.04 411.63 157.81 414.5 176.97 C 417.38 196.14 420.25 217.71 423.13 241.66 C 426 265.62 428.88 291.98 431.75 320.73\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#247456\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\" stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"53.97\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">y = -x² + 4<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"359.3,103.37 400.7,103.37\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#d0a64a\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"95.37\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">x‑axis<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"359.3,103.37 359.3,103.37\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#277da1\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"359.3\\\" y=\\\"95.37\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">Root x = -2<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"400.7,103.37 400.7,103.37\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#c85845\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"400.7\\\" y=\\\"95.37\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">Root x = 2<\\/text><\\/g><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"377\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">x<\\/text><text x=\\\"12\\\" y=\\\"181\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\" transform=\\\"rotate(-90 12 181)\\\">y<\\/text><\\/svg><\\/div><p>Students are given the equation -x² + 4 = 0. They sketch the graph, identify the intercepts, and then verify the solutions using the quadratic formula.<\\/p><\\/article><article class=\\\"presentation-slide-preview presentation-theme-modern presentation-template-lesson\\\"><header><span>SLIDE 08<\\/span><small>Mathematics · SHS Year 3<\\/small><\\/header><h4>Slide 8 – Real‑Life Application: Projectile Motion<\\/h4><ul><li>A projectile’s height h(t) can be modelled by h(t) = -5t² + 20t + 1 (t in seconds).<\\/li><li>The range of t for which h(t) &gt; 0 gives the flight time.<\\/li><li>The vertex gives the maximum height and the time at which it occurs.<\\/li><\\/ul><div class=\\\"presentation-visual presentation-visual-geometry\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><strong>Lesson visual<\\/strong><svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 720 380\\\" role=\\\"img\\\" aria-label=\\\"Lesson visual\\\"><defs><clipPath id=\\\"geometry-clip-9ofs2lwn9n\\\"><rect x=\\\"362.93\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" width=\\\"34.13\\\" height=\\\"314\\\"\\/><\\/clipPath><\\/defs><line x1=\\\"362.93\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"362.93\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"362.93\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"397.07\\\" y2=\\\"24\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"362.93\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-0.31<\\/text><text x=\\\"354.93\\\" y=\\\"28\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">24.84<\\/text><line x1=\\\"371.47\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"371.47\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"362.93\\\" y1=\\\"102.5\\\" x2=\\\"397.07\\\" y2=\\\"102.5\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"371.47\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">1.1<\\/text><text x=\\\"354.93\\\" y=\\\"106.5\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">11.92<\\/text><line x1=\\\"380\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"380\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"362.93\\\" y1=\\\"181\\\" x2=\\\"397.07\\\" y2=\\\"181\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">2.5<\\/text><text x=\\\"354.93\\\" y=\\\"185\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-1<\\/text><line x1=\\\"388.53\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"388.53\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"362.93\\\" y1=\\\"259.5\\\" x2=\\\"397.07\\\" y2=\\\"259.5\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"388.53\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">3.9<\\/text><text x=\\\"354.93\\\" y=\\\"263.5\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-13.92<\\/text><line x1=\\\"397.07\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"397.07\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"362.93\\\" y1=\\\"338\\\" x2=\\\"397.07\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-grid\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"397.07\\\" y=\\\"354\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">5.31<\\/text><text x=\\\"354.93\\\" y=\\\"342\\\" text-anchor=\\\"end\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">-26.84<\\/text><line x1=\\\"364.81\\\" y1=\\\"24\\\" x2=\\\"364.81\\\" y2=\\\"338\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-axis\\\"\\/><line x1=\\\"362.93\\\" y1=\\\"174.92\\\" x2=\\\"397.07\\\" y2=\\\"174.92\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-axis\\\"\\/><g clip-path=\\\"url(#geometry-clip-9ofs2lwn9n)\\\"><path d=\\\"M 364.81 168.85 C 365.66 151.97 366.5 136.86 367.34 123.5 C 368.19 110.14 369.03 98.53 369.87 88.69 C 370.72 78.85 371.56 70.76 372.41 64.43 C 373.25 58.1 374.09 53.53 374.94 50.72 C 375.78 47.91 376.62 46.85 377.47 47.56 C 378.31 48.26 379.16 50.72 380 54.94 C 380.84 59.16 381.69 65.14 382.53 72.87 C 383.38 80.6 384.22 90.1 385.06 101.35 C 385.91 112.6 386.75 125.61 387.59 140.37 C 388.44 155.14 389.28 171.66 390.13 189.94 C 390.97 208.23 391.81 228.27 392.66 250.06 C 393.5 271.86 394.34 295.42 395.19 320.73\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#247456\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\" stroke-linecap=\\\"round\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"46.94\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">h(t) = -5t² + 20t + 1<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"364.81,174.92 395.19,174.92\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#d0a64a\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"166.92\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">ground (h = 0)<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"376.96,174.92 376.96,174.92\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#277da1\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"376.96\\\" y=\\\"166.92\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">Landing time ≈ 4.0 s<\\/text><polyline points=\\\"376.96,47.35 376.96,47.35\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#c85845\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2.5\\\"\\/><text x=\\\"376.96\\\" y=\\\"39.35\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-shape-label\\\">Maximum height ≈ 21 m<\\/text><\\/g><text x=\\\"380\\\" y=\\\"377\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\">time (s)<\\/text><text x=\\\"12\\\" y=\\\"181\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" class=\\\"presentation-geometry-label\\\" transform=\\\"rotate(-90 12 181)\\\">height (m)<\\/text><\\/svg><\\/div><p>Groups calculate the flight time by finding where h(t) = 0 using the graph. They also identify the time of maximum height and discuss practical implications (e.g., when a ball lands).<\\/p><\\/article><\\/div><\\/div><div class=\\\"document-section\\\"><h3>Teacher lecture notes · private<\\/h3><ol><li><strong>Slide 1:<\\/strong> Explain that the coefficients are chosen for illustration only; the focus is on recognising the quadratic form and its curved shape. Emphasise how the sign of \\\\(a\\\\) determines opening upward or downward.<\\/li><li><strong>Slide 2:<\\/strong> Guide learners to calculate the vertex (0,0) and show that the axis passes through it. Highlight that the axis formula gives the same result for this simple case.<\\/li><li><strong>Slide 3:<\\/strong> Show algebraic solution: set \\\\(x^2 - 4 = 2x + 1\\\\) → \\\\(x^2 - 2x -5 = 0\\\\). Use quadratic formula to find \\\\(x = 1 \\\\pm \\\\sqrt{6}\\\\). Mark these points on the graph to confirm.<\\/li><li><strong>Slide 4:<\\/strong> Walk students through each row, emphasizing how the axis tells us the vertex occurs at the centre (x = 0). Highlight that the linear condition simply fixes a point on the graph to evaluate.<\\/li><li><strong>Slide 5:<\\/strong> Explain the vertex formula h = -b\\/(2a). For f(x) = -x² + 4, h = 0, so the vertex is at (0,4). Emphasise that because a is negative, the parabola opens downward, making the vertex a maximum. Use the plotted graph to illustrate that as x moves right from 0, y decreases, and as x moves left from 0, y also decreases, highlighting the opposite directions of increase\\/decrease relative to the vertex.<\\/li><li><strong>Slide 6:<\\/strong> Derive the intercepts by solving -x² + 4 = 0 → x² = 4 → x = ±2. Highlight that for -2 &lt; x &lt; 2, the parabola lies above the x‑axis (y &gt; 0). Outside this interval, y becomes negative. Relate this to real‑world contexts such as the height of a thrown ball being above ground only between launch and landing points.<\\/li><li><strong>Slide 7:<\\/strong> Walk through the steps: (1) Set y = 0, (2) Plot the parabola, (3) Read off the x‑coordinates where the curve meets the x‑axis. Show the quadratic formula x = [-b ± √(b²‑4ac)]\\/(2a) with a = -1, b = 0, c = 4, yielding x = ±2. Emphasise that the graphical method provides a visual check on the algebraic result.<\\/li><li><strong>Slide 8:<\\/strong> Explain that the coefficients come from physics (gravity ≈ -10 m\\/s², simplified to -5 for the model). Use the quadratic formula to find roots: t = [‑20 ± √(400‑20)]\\/(‑10) → t ≈ 0.05 s and t ≈ 4.0 s (ignore the tiny initial root). The vertex occurs at t = -b\\/(2a) = 2 s, giving h(2) = 21 m. Discuss how the graph instantly shows the time interval (0.05 s &lt; t &lt; 4.0 s) where the ball is above ground.<\\/li><\\/ol><p>These notes are for the teacher and are not shared on student presentation screens.<\\/p><\\/div><div class=\\\"output-warning\\\">Export the editable PowerPoint deck to present or further edit. Review curriculum alignment, data and examples before classroom use.<\\/div><\\/div><\\/article>\"}','2026-11-01 01:57:54','2026-11-01 06:42:02'),
