":\"Use verified curriculum resources from these selected SHS years: SHS3.\\nUse only these selected weekly sections as the assessment scope: SHS3, Term Semester 1, Week 10: Identify parts of a circle and draw circles for given radii and through points.\"},\"assessment_draft\":{\"title\":\"MATHS QUIZ 1\",\"instructions\":\"Answer all questions.\",\"questions\":[{\"prompt\":\"In the diagram below, O is the centre of the circle and P lies on the circumference. Which line segment represents a radius of the circle?\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"OP\",\"PQ\",\"OC\",\"AB\"],\"correct_option\":0,\"visual\":{\"type\":\"geometry\",\"x_min\":-5,\"x_max\":5,\"y_min\":-5,\"y_max\":5,\"shapes\":[{\"shape\":\"circle\",\"label\":\"\",\"center\":[0,0],\"radius\":4},{\"shape\":\"line\",\"label\":\"OP\",\"points\":[[0,0],[4,0]]}],\"title\":\"Circle with centre O and point P on circumference\",\"x_label\":\"\",\"y_label\":\"\"}},{\"prompt\":\"A circle has a radius of 5 cm. What is its circumference? (Use π ≈ 3.14)\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"10π cm\",\"5π cm\",\"20π cm\",\"15π cm\"],\"correct_option\":0},{\"question_number\":1,\"prompt\":\"In the diagram below, line segment AB joins two points on the circle. What is the correct term for AB?\",\"visual\":{\"type\":\"geometry\",\"x_min\":0,\"x_max\":10,\"y_min\":0,\"y_max\":10,\"shapes\":[{\"shape\":\"circle\",\"label\":\"O\",\"center\":[5,5],\"radius\":4},{\"shape\":\"line\",\"label\":\"AB\",\"points\":[[3,5],[7,5]]}],\"title\":\"Circle Diagram\",\"x_label\":\"\",\"y_label\":\"\"},\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"Radius\",\"Diameter\",\"Chord\",\"Tangent\"],\"correct_option\":2},{\"question_number\":2,\"prompt\":\"A circle is drawn with centre O and radius 5 cm. Which of the following statements is correct?\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"The diameter of the circle is 5 cm.\",\"The circumference of the circle is 10π cm.\",\"The area of the circle is 5π cm².\",\"A line from O to any point on the circle is called a chord.\"],\"correct_option\":1},{\"question_number\":1,\"prompt\":\"In the diagram below, which label corresponds to the radius of the circle?\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"Diameter\",\"Chord\",\"Radius\",\"Tangent\"],\"correct_option\":2,\"expected_answer\":\"Radius\",\"visual\":{\"type\":\"geometry\",\"x_min\":-5,\"x_max\":5,\"y_min\":-5,\"y_max\":5,\"shapes\":[{\"shape\":\"circle\",\"label\":\"circle\",\"center\":[0,0],\"radius\":3},{\"shape\":\"line\",\"label\":\"radius\",\"points\":[[0,0],[3,0]]},{\"shape\":\"line\",\"label\":\"diameter\",\"points\":[[-3,0],[3,0]]},{\"shape\":\"line\",\"label\":\"chord\",\"points\":[[0,3],[0,-3]]}],\"title\":\"Circle with labeled parts\",\"x_label\":\"\",\"y_label\":\"\"}},{\"question_number\":2,\"prompt\":\"A circle is to be drawn with centre at (2, -1) and passing through the point (5, 3). What is the radius of the circle?\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"6\"],\"correct_option\":2,\"expected_answer\":\"5\"},{\"prompt\":\"Which term describes the line segment that passes through the centre of a circle and whose endpoints lie on the circle?\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"Radius\",\"Diameter\",\"Chord\",\"Tangent\"],\"correct_option\":1},{\"prompt\":\"A circle has centre O at the origin (0,0) and passes through point A(3,4). What is the radius of the circle?\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"5 cm\",\"7 cm\",\"3 cm\",\"4 cm\"],\"correct_option\":0,\"visual\":{\"type\":\"geometry\",\"x_min\":-6,\"x_max\":6,\"y_min\":-6,\"y_max\":6,\"shapes\":[{\"shape\":\"circle\",\"label\":\"O\",\"center\":[0,0],\"radius\":5},{\"shape\":\"circle\",\"label\":\"A\",\"center\":[3,4],\"radius\":0.2}],\"title\":\"Circle with centre O and point A\",\"x_label\":\"\",\"y_label\":\"\"}},{\"question_number\":1,\"prompt\":\"Which term describes the line segment that joins the centre of a circle to any point on the circle?\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"Radius\",\"Diameter\",\"Chord\",\"Tangent\"],\"correct_option\":0},{\"question_number\":2,\"prompt\":\"A circle has its centre at point O(2,3) and a radius of 5 cm. Which equation correctly represents this circle?\",\"question_type\":\"mcq\",\"marks\":5,\"options\":[\"(x-2)^2 + (y-3)^2 = 25\",\"(x+2)^2 + (y-3)^2 = 25\",\"(x-2)^2 + (y+3)^2 = 25\",\"(x+2)^2 + (y+3)^2 = 25\"],\"correct_option\":0}],\"marking_guide\":[{\"question_number\":1,\"expected_response\":\"OP\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":2,\"expected_response\":\"10π cm\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":3,\"expected_response\":\"Chord\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":4,\"expected_response\":\"The circumference of the circle is 10π cm.\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":5,\"expected_response\":\"Radius\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":6,\"expected_response\":\"5\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":7,\"expected_response\":\"Diameter\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":8,\"expected_response\":\"5 cm\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":9,\"expected_response\":\"Radius\",\"marks\":5},{\"question_number\":10,\"expected_response\":\"(x-2)^2 + (y-3)^2 = 25\",\"marks\":5}],\"curriculum_outline\":[\"Strand: 1. Numbers for Everyday Life\",\"Sub-strand: 2. Proportional Reasoning\",\"Strand: 2. Algebraic Reasoning\",\"Sub-strand: 2. Patterns and Relationships\",\"Strand: 3. Geometry Around Us\",\"Sub-strand: 1. Spatial Sense\",\"Sub-strand: 2. Measurement\",\"Strand: 4. Making Sense of and Using Data\",\"Sub-strand: 1. Statistical Reasoning and Its Application in Real Life\",\"Sub-strand: 2. Probability\\/Chance\"],\"total_marks\":50,\"curriculum_outline_status\":\"available\",\"curriculum_outline_source_url\":\"https:\\/\\/nacca.gov.gh\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2025\\/04\\/Mathematics-Curriculum.pdf\",\"curriculum_sources\":[{\"document_id\":1,\"chunk_id\":147,\"title\":\"Mathematics_Y3_TM_ONLINE-VERSION_FINAL.