(4,1,'slides','Investigating Partial Variation · presentation outline','Mathematics','SHS3',NULL,'draft','{\"type\":\"slides\",\"year_group\":\"SHS3\",\"subject\":\"Mathematics\",\"class_name\":\"\",\"teacher_instructions\":\"Use a inquiry and discovery structure.\\nCover every selected weekly section across the presentation; use the selected_week_sections data as the source of the week-by-week scope.\\nKeep the outline editable, age-appropriate, classroom-ready, and grounded in the supplied topics and teacher-editable outcomes, indicators and teaching points. Do not invent official curriculum wording.\\nInclude concise lecture notes in each slide\'s private presenter_notes field. Incorporate supplied teacher notes, and never place presenter notes in student-facing slide content.\",\"topic\":\"Use proportional reasoning to investigate partial variations, make generalisations and solve\",\"selected_week_sections\":[{\"semester_number\":1,\"week_number\":5,\"topic\":\"Use proportional reasoning to investigate partial variations, make generalisations and solve\",\"strand\":\"NUMBERS FOR EVERYDAY LIFE\",\"sub_strand\":\"Proportional Reasoning\",\"content_standard\":\"Demonstrate conceptual understanding of proportionality in relation to variation and use it to solve real-life problems.\",\"focal_areas\":[\"Variation 2\",\"VARIATION 2\"],\"learning_indicators\":[\"Use proportional reasoning to investigate partial variations, make generalisations and solve real-life issues involving partial variations\"],\"learning_outcomes\":[],\"source_title\":\"Mathematics_Y3_TM_ONLINE-VERSION_FINAL.pdf\",\"source_reference\":\"MOE Verified\",\"source_page\":27}],\"presentation_template\":\"inquiry\",\"presentation_visual_theme\":\"vibrant\",\"presentation_outcomes\":\"\",\"presentation_indicators\":\"\",\"teaching_points\":[],\"presentation_visual_data\":\"\",\"presentation_lecture_notes\":\"\",\"number_of_slides\":14,\"year\":\"SHS Year 3\",\"title\":\"Investigating Partial Variation\",\"template\":\"inquiry\",\"visual_theme\":\"vibrant\",\"selected_weeks\":[{\"semester_number\":1,\"week_number\":5,\"topic\":\"Use proportional reasoning to investigate partial variations, make generalisations and solve\",\"strand\":\"NUMBERS FOR EVERYDAY LIFE\",\"sub_strand\":\"Proportional Reasoning\",\"content_standard\":\"Demonstrate conceptual understanding of proportionality in relation to variation and use it to solve real-life problems.\",\"focal_areas\":[\"Variation 2\",\"VARIATION 2\"],\"learning_indicators\":[\"Use proportional reasoning to investigate partial variations, make generalisations and solve real-life issues involving partial variations\"],\"learning_outcomes\":[],\"source_title\":\"Mathematics_Y3_TM_ONLINE-VERSION_FINAL.pdf\",\"source_reference\":\"MOE Verified\",\"source_page\":27}],\"learning_outcomes\":[],\"learning_indicators\":[],\"visual_data\":\"\",\"slides\":[{\"title\":\"What is Partial Variation?\",\"key_points\":[\"A relationship with a fixed component (c) and a variable component (k·x)\",\"Graph shifts upward; does not pass through the origin\",\"Common in fees that include a base charge plus usage\"],\"activity\":\"Students list everyday costs that combine a base fee with a usage charge.\",\"visual_suggestion\":\"\",\"visual\":null,\"presenter_notes\":\"Introduce the term \'partial variation\' from the curriculum excerpt. Emphasise the constant term c and relate it to real‑life examples like a monthly subscription fee plus per‑unit usage. Prompt students to think of other scenarios.\",\"image\":{\"url\":\"data:image\\/jpeg;base64,\\/9j\\/4AAQSkZJRgABAQAASABIAAD\\/4QBMRXhpZgAATU0AKgAAAAgAAYdpAAQAAAABAAAAGgAAAAAAA6ABAAMAAAABAAEAAKACAAQAAAABAAAC9KADAAQAAAABAAAB+AAAAAD\\/7QA4UGhvdG9zaG9wIDMuMAA4QklNBAQAAAAAAAA4QklNBCUAAAAAABDUHYzZjwCyBOmACZjs+EJ+\\/8AAEQgB+AL0AwEiAAIRAQMRAf\\/EAB8AAAEFAQEBAQEBAAAAAAAAAAABAgMEBQYHCAkKC\\/\\/EALUQAAIBAwMCBAMFBQQEAAABfQECAwAEEQUSITFBBhNRYQcicRQygZGhCCNCscEVUtHwJDNicoIJChYXGBkaJSYnKCkqNDU2Nzg5OkNERUZHS